{ The so-called Classical system. White just wants to complete his development, without any intentions of a kingside attack. It is a decent option that gives White a fine position with a little more space, but Black does get a dream Sicilian, with pressure along the long diagonal and the c-file. We develop our pieces naturally, bring out the knight to c6, and the c8-bishop either gets employed on b7 (after a6 and b5) or on the d7/e6-squares. }
