{ It is certainly possible and highly interesting to investigate the slower lines starting with Bd7 and then Rc8 or Rb8. But while some of that is certainly a lot of fun, Black will experience some theoretical difficulties if White knows what he is doing, and it is certainly one of the reasons why the Dragon has faded away from high-level practice. With the line I would like to suggest, I propose to challenge this status quo and solve our opening problems in a very straightforward fashion. It is certainly possible and highly interesting to investigate the slower lines starting with Bd7 and then Rc8 or Rb8. But while some of that is certainly a lot of fun, Black is experiencing some theoretical difficulties if White knows what he is doing, and it is certainly one of the reasons why the Dragon has faded away from high-level practice. With the line I would like to suggest, I propose to challenge this status quo and solve our opening problems in a very straightforward fashion. }
