11... fxe6 12. O-O-O
{ White has to castle long if he wants to get anything in this particular line, but also in the Dragon in general. Our only fundamental issue is a potentially vulnerable king. If White were to castle short here 12.O-O we would just get the queen out with 12...Qa5 , trade the d4-bishop after Nd7 or Nh5 and enjoy the pressure along the c-file. The c3-knight would be particularly aimless with the pawn on e6 guarding the d5-square. 12.h4 here or on the next move will transpose to the12.O-O-O move order, after for example 12...Qa5 13.O-O-O Rac8 14.Kb1 . }
12... Da5
